important  and  elements  in  an  experimental  design  we  thought  w ould  help  in 
materializing objective phenomena. I sought to employ a diffractive approach in 
the intra-active discussion between the students and me. This involved using each 
students’ suggestions arranged with, against and through each other has to highlight 
differences in their ideas and possibi lities that could ensue. Simply put, I allowed 
students  to  suggest  apparatus  and  protocols  they  would  use  to  test  the  effect 
of  ocean  acidity  on  shells  and   using  a  combination of  layering their  suggestions 
upon each other, combining their suggestions and talking through them, looked for 
highlighted  areas of difference and superposition. In this process, the apparatus for 
experimentation included (at various times) slides of an experimental set-up I placed 
in front of them, their own  laptops used as resources, materials in the classroom 
