(like race and colorism, gender and sexuality, implications of socioeconomic status 
and privilege) that are layered with deep emotions ( could be positive or negative) and 
tend to be more closely aligned with the vulnerabilities of questioning assumptions 
about identity, “place” in so ciety, and the emotional valences inextricably associated 
