3.1.2 
The  socio-pragmatic  theory  describes  social  cognitive  development  and 
defines behaviours related to social an d language development during the first 
years of life (Tomasello, 1999/2003). Social and language development begin 
when the individual understands others as beings with mental and intentional 
states, just like him- or herself . Thus, an understanding of the self and others 
as intentional agents whose behavioural and attentional strategies are organ-
ised based on goals emerg es. When the child understands that intentionality 

