"In historical and cultural terms, what does the Mongolian concept of khot ail describe, and how has it been applied in a modern setting involving an NGO?","Teachers shared stories of morally 
nurturing experiences with and for students. Moral education transferred from 
scheduled classroom lessons into relationships. The positive flow of power in 
the teacher-student relationship went both ways. Teachers noticed the awak-
ening of internal discipline and motivation within the students. One teacher 
reflected that “once the heart is involved it becomes pure – it is with virtues 
language” (Hancock, 2015, p. 240). Relationships within a group having iluu oir 
dotno is a condition of khot ail, which in historical and cultural terms refers to 
several ger families  having relational and economic closeness. This is a highly 
valued way of being together for Mongolians. There are examples of the appli-
