What is identified as the primary responsibility of a learning companion when helping employees engage with informal learning in a corporate setting?,"This  is  meant  to  be  more  of  a  function  than  a  person,  be-
cause the tasks of the learning companion can be carried out 
by one person, but  are often distributed across several shoul-
ders  in  larger  companies:  personnel,  management  and  (for-
mer) trainers. 6.1.1    Performance Clarify

Sometimes  the  introduction  of  informal  learning  formats  is 
commented  on  with  statements  like  “We’re  saving   a  lot  of 
money here if we don’t have to use expensive external train-
ers!” The argument of (possible) cost reduction is of course a 
bad advisor . Because what is decisive is whether the desired, 
informal learning also provides a real benefit, that is, whether 
it provides assistance in solving  performance problems. If this 
relevance is lacking, this learning format is very likely not to 
be  used  by  the  learners. This  then  ultimately  saves  no  costs, 
but “burns” often not inconsiderable sums. It  is  therefore  the  task  of  the  learning  companion  to 
bring  about  a  detailed  clarification  of  the  performance  with 
all stakeholders . Here he acts more as a consultant who, for 
example, works out in moderated workshops how the learn-
ing  strategy  fits  the  corporate  strategy. The  learning  com-
panion can, for example, create competence profiles together 
with the employees and management, which show who needs 
which  comp etences  for  the  performance  of  his  performance 
and  what  is  needed  in  order  to  acquire  them  through  infor-
mal learning. 6.1.2    Supporting Learners

