Informal learning also requires a climate that is characterized 
by trust and tolerance for mistakes. Because only then do em-
ployees dare to ask each other for support and thus show that 
they  do  not  know  or  can  do  something. Tolerance  for  mis-
takes  also  supports  a  Working-Out-Loud  practice,  because 
even sharing work results requires courage. Answering ques-
tions  such  as  “Is  the  sight  of  an  (learning)  employee  with 
headphones accepted or does it suggest that he is not work-
ing,  but rather ‘private pleasures’ are being pursued?” or “Is 
an employee who spends a lot of time passing on his knowl-
edge to other employees accused  of not doing enough?” can 
give clues to the current learning culture. z  Developing competencies
Developing  a  learning  culture  also  includes  the  question  of 
which  competencies  need  to  be  present  within  th e  organiza-
