will  have  a  higher  life  expectancy. –  There   might   be   no   connections   between   two   variables   and   still   we   find   a  
(spurious)  correlation. There  are  many  examples  of  this  effect;;  one  could  look  
for  any  two  variables  changing  in  time. The  two  variables  are  then  correlated  –  
but  without  any  reason. Fitting  models  to  bivariate  data  
