transnational arrangements. The push for transnational higher education found an 
economic  rationale  in  recent  scholarships  on  internationalization. Maringe  and 
Gibbs (2009) found that universities with high levels of internationalization attract 
more  foreign  staff  and  students,  contribute   more  to  local  and  regional  economic 
development, but  also  have  high  annual income turnovers  and  highly diversified 
income generating sou rces. TRANSNATIONAL PULL

