What reason is given for the removal of Julia Alvarez's novel In the Time of the Butterflies from circulation in certain Georgia counties?,"(p. 20)

 “Becoming different” has no value in our society. There is fear in becoming different. Different is unpredictable and frightening; different is, well, different. The hidden 
curriculum encourages us to fit in. We teach our students, whether intentionally or 
not, that same is good and that preserving traditions, routines, and attitudes is the way 
to strengt hen our communities and thus ourselves by participating. This difference 
is  part  of  becoming  a  self  or  an  individual  through,  as  Greene  says,  “envisaged 
possibility,” that is made possible thr ough avenues such as poetry writing or even 
understanding poetry by others through different “unaccustomed angles.” 

