CHAP TER 6

The Reality of English Language Teaching and 
Learning at Rural Telesecundarias in Mexico

Arely Romero García and Leticia Araceli Salas Serran o

Abstract

Education has always been a polemic topic for experts and non-experts, and  Mexican 
instruction is no exception. According to Solís (2017, in Lakhani, 2017, para. 20), educa-
tion can be a vehicle for social mobility, but it can also reflect and reproduce inequali-
ties, as it happens in most Mexican schools. This is the case of rural Telesecundarias, the 
schools in Mexico which deliver instruction through a televised system. This chapter 
attempts to identify educational challenges in English classes at rural  Telesecundarias 
in Mexico from the perspective of a group of t eachers and students in this context and 
how these challenges can turn into opportunities to offer equal access to education 
in rural areas. To collect information, structured interviews were conducted to iden-
tify the participants’ views. The analysis of the data concluded that opportunities in 
English education might be the same for all Mexican students. Nevertheless, there is 
a crucial need to adapt programs, enhance teachers’ updating and commitment, and, 
most of all, consider rural Telesecundarias  equal to other schools in the country. The 
researchers and interviewees hope these actions may lead to the effective implemen-
tation of English instruction in this rural setting. Keywords

education in Mexico – rural – Telesecundarias – English teaching and learning – edu-
cational challenges

