The contours of the emerging society with a high participation higher edu-
cation system are only starting to appear. There is no clear pathway to reflect 
on the changes in a society with a high participation higher education system. Therefore, this chapter will approach the task from different disciplinary per-
spectives. First, it will ask: what do we know about the role of higher educa-
tion in society? To answer the question, the chapter will consider insights from 
social theories best positioned to explore the social dimensions. Second, it will 
ask: what do we know about the nature of higher education? This is a question 
for the philosophy of education. Third, the chapter will suggest some insights 
about the emerging society in which the majority have higher education, and 
some directions for future  lines of research inquiry. 2 

What Do We Know about the Role of Higher Education in Society? Higher education has not been a traditional focus of sociology since its emer-
gence as a discipline. Arguably, until quite recently, when higher education was 
still not a mass and large-scale institution of society, social sciences preferred 

