concern an entire class of mathematical objects or situations without  exceptions. Particular statements refer to a statement that concerns a speciﬁc mathematical
object or situation. A general statement with particular instantiation concerns an
entire class of mathematical objects but for which a speciﬁc member of the class has
bee n selected for students’ use in reasoning (Otten et al., 2014). This type of
statement can be considered an exemplar or a generic example (Balacheff, 1988) of

