•  subsequent  monitoring  of  the  development  of  the  situation. The  simulators  allow  each  specialist  to  imitate  the  management  of  the 
technological  equipment  entrusted  to  him. Moreover,  the  engineer  can 
work  with  the  main  server  of  the  system  and  its  information  databases 
and  interact  with  other  members   of  the  team. The  system  also  allows 
the  trainees  to  receive  and  to  transmit  service  information,  orders,  etc. to  the  senior  manager. All  production  or  design  issues  are  formulated 
in  such  a  way  that  it  is  not  possible  to  solve  them  by  the  efforts  of  only 
one   specialist. It  is  caused  by  heterogeneity  of  the  initial  information,  the 
necessity  to  use  specialized  software  and  interdisciplinary  discussion. The 
joint  training  is  attended  by  the  students  of  various  ﬁelds  of  study. They 
take  on  the  roles  of  a  geophysicist,  a  geologist,  a  driller,  a  developer,  a 
production  technologist  and  an  economist  respecti vely. Moreover,  about 
half  of  the  classroom  time  is  allocated  for  the  joint  trainings  to  resolve  the 
conﬂict  issues,  agree  on  decisions   and  select  the  recommended  options. The  leaders  of  the  “company”  or  “department”  are  selected  in  each  team 
of  students. One  of  the  tasks  of  the  leader  is  to  determine  the  responsi-
bilities  of  each  team  member,  depending  on  the  selected  case. At  the  end 
of  the  lesson,  the  teams  of  students  present  their  programs,  justifying 
and  defending  their  decisions  in  front  of  othe r  competing  teams. When 
evaluating  the  results  of  each  team,  the  following  criteria  are  considered: 
the  validity  of  the  decisions  made,  the  speciﬁc  e conomic  beneﬁt  from  the 
proposed  solution  and  the  activity  of  the  team. Interdisciplinary Training in the Virtual Environment …

