The  major  purpose  of  any  educational  system  includes  obtaining 
a  qualiﬁcation  as  an  engineer  or  a  master  of  science  by  ac quisition 
of  professional  competencies  and  skills  that  are  in  high  demand  by 
employers. However,  the  key  objective  of  education  is  providing  knowl-
edge  that  will  be  relevant  tomorrow. The  leading  industrial  compa-
nies  require  specialists  with  a  wide  range  of  technical  and  academical 
knowledge  and  experience  of  wor king  in  a  team  and  making  coordi-
nated  decisions. This  approach  was  bequeathed  to  the  university  by  the 
academician  Ivan  Gubkin,  the  founder  of  the  oil  and  gas  university 
named  af ter  him. Ivan  Gubkin  was  an  outstanding  petroleum  scientist 
and  the  founder  of  petroleum  education  in  Russia. His  position  about 
education  in  the  petroleum  industry  was  based  on  an  interdisciplinary 
approach:  “If  we  strive  to  comprehend  the   nature  of  petroleum  ﬁelds,  it 
is  essential  that  the  geologist,  the  chemist  and  the  physicist  walk  hand  in 
hand,  mutually  learning   from  each  other”  (Koshelev  et  al. 2020). Interdisciplinary Training in the Virtual Environment …

