the typical person (DSM-IV). This diversity of proﬁles causes multiple challenges
in terms of methodologies and teaching programs directed towards autistic children. This is the reason why we believe that modeling affect is the proper approach for ISLA to
teach mathematics to children with autism. 2.4

Intelligent Tutoring Systems (ITS) and Affect Management

An ITS is a computer system designed with the objective of providing instant and
custom ized instruction or feedback to learners. This is generally done without

