A.L. Mondragon et al. intervention from a human teacher, and with the intention of enabling learning in a
meaningful effective way by using a variety of computing technolog ies [26], Many
ITSs have been developed and are being used in different domains in formal education
(i.e. Auto Tutor [15], ANDES [33], among others). Some ITSs exist for corporate and
industry training, including SHERLOCK [19], all of which have demonstrated their
capabilities and limitations. Researchers claim that if computers are to interact naturally
with humans, they must also be able to recognize, affect and express social compe-
tenci es [27]. The ‘affective’ approach within intelligent tutoring system has been val-
idated as having a positive impact on the learner’s intuition, and on his/he r self-esteem,
as it relates to problem solving tasks [9, 24]. Thus ‘cognition’, ‘motivation’ and
‘emotional affect’ are three components of learning [13]. In [2], they have demonstrated
different sensors that can be used to detect emotions during a learning session such as
