error and where to focus the subsequent learning activity [30]. For instance, [34]
suggests a mechanism to cognitive diagnoses dealing with ‘behavioral’ description, and
adaptation used in AutoTutor [15], and Andes  [33]. Reference [1] outlines the
importance of the models’ ‘ﬂexibility’ and its cognitive ‘ﬁdelity’. In [3] they examined
the effectiveness of pedagogical agents (PAs’) with MetaTutor for the purpose of
training students on self-regulated learning (SR L) processes to cognitive diagnosis
through prompting and providing feedback that facilitated learning about the human
circulatory system. 3 System Overview and Pedagogical Methodology

