2.2

Specialized Education in Autism

Reference [11], have developed the ‘Cognitiv e Assessment System’ used in the
understanding, assessment and diagnosis in the intervention of different educational
problems like autism, reading di sabilities, attention deﬁcit disorder, etc. Most teaching
and learning approaches to autism have a tendency to integrate a variety of educational
and psycho educational programs from the discipl ines of behaviorism and psychology
[23]. The goal is to tackle three main aspects of intervention among children with
autism. The ﬁrst deals with communication and social interaction; the second with
developmental and educational strategies. The last one deals with behavioral tech-
niques to improve learning and behavior. Research in autism has proven that early
intervention is fundamental to any child on the spectrum. Some forms of early inter-
vention include physical and social therapy, Applied Behavioral Analysis (ABA), and
speech-therapy. For instance, ABA approach and Verbal Behavior are drawn on the
research and theories of [29]. Other approaches, to tackle the issue of social commu-
nication impairments faced by children with ASD, have been made by using virtual
reality techno logies [20]. In this research, we propose an affective intelligent tutoring
system ISLA to detect and appropriately respond to the affective state of an ASD
learne r in a mathematical situation. With these concepts in mind, the question to ask is:
As human beings, do we all have metacognitive capabilities that enable us to adapt and
respond to  our environment? The answer is that most metacognitive skills that we take
for granted are poor or absent in children with autism. 2.3 Emotions and Autism

