alarming  escalation  of  behavioral  disruption  in  school  display ed  in  alternating 
incidents  of  aggression  and  withdrawal. Despite  repeated  attempts  by  teachers 
and school counselors to discuss his concerns, Matt refused to disclose any of his 
thoughts or feelings re lated to these school incidents, nor did he acknowledge his 
recent disturbing behavioral escalation. During this time, Matt attended his regular 
Young Warriors program sessions. In one of these sessions, Matt and the other group 
participants were shown a Rap video by the Geto Boys called “Six Feet Deep.” This 
somber video de picted a young man who was walking peacefully with his group 
of friends, but was suddenly murdered by random gunfire. The video emphasized 
images of grief-stricken family and friends attending the subsequent young man’s 
funeral, and the program participants in this  specific group were visibly moved by 
explicit displays of vulnerable emotions by the male youth – who typically deny or 
dismiss vulnerable emotions  in the presence of their peers to maintain their “macho” 
self-image. Additionally,  the  video  depicts  a  crowd  of  black  suits,  attending  the 
funeral as the camera pans across the lonely and grief-stricken faces  of the church 
community in mourning. Another camera angle shot shows the view of looking up 
from the casket, which is buried six feet deep into the ground. Other questions that 
were posed are related to, “who might be to blame for this tragedy?” as well as “who 
are real friends?”

