improvement  in  the  spaces  of  the  dormitory  and  day  centre  for  homeless. It  has 
supported the educational project in the production of forms of self-management of 
the service. It has increased the awareness that occupational laboratories, already 
existing in the structure, could result in original and authorial languages. It has given 
a  group  of  students  the  chance  to  make  use  of  untraditional  forms  of  education, 
which have enabled a direct engagement wit h reality. The  event,  a  design  workshop  coordinated  by  the  anthroplogist  Valentina 
