key role in noticing a child’s need for intensified support, the multidisciplinary stu-
dent welfare team helps t o confirm the decision. The plan also includes detailed 
information on the preparation process, on the guardians’ and the child’s hearing, 
and on the documents used in the  process. Finally, the plan also must include infor-
mation on the revision of the plan. The plan needs to be revised at least once a year 
or whenever there is a need to make modifications due to changes in the child’s 
needs or condition . 162

