dence that subjective values or ethical properties “were not stimulated by 
perception of an objective pr operty”. the concepts of culture and ‘Knowledge’

When delving into Chinese theorising, culture is perceived from both nar-
row and broad perspectives. For example, ‘c-ulture’ (Qian 2011) contains 
the knowledge humans developed, that can be learned and used to change 
the world. This is knowledge for knowledge’s sake that is acquired through 
education. A ‘c-ultured’ person is a ‘knowledgeable’ person in terms of 
knowing  literature,  formulas  and  problem  solving,  philosophy  and  the 
skills of  deduction with corresponding links to Li’s (2016) ‘人化’ (renhua: 
humans transform). A ‘C-ultured’ person (Qian 2011) not only has mas-
tery over a significant knowledge base but also has the power to transform 
that knowledge to spiri tually2 lift him or herself to a higher level of exis-
tence. This is similar to Li’s (2016) ‘化人’ (huaren: transform humans). When the knowledge people have learned has resulted in an internalised 
change in their thinking and acting (e.g. humanely), ‘C-ulture’ is realised. Culture is often regarded as having an emotional nucleus constituted 
by spiritual enlightenment forged by philosophers throughout its history. Chinese culture is viewed as specifically pursuing a spiritual path and plac-
ing morality and sensibility in a lofty position (Yue 2016, p. 318). In con-
trast with ‘knowledge’ based on rationality and cognition, culture does 
not appear to have a scientific basis (Yue 2016, p. 311). So how is culture 
related  to  knowledge  or  the  knowledgeable  person? Can  culture  or 
Chinese culture be classified using the concepts by which knowledge is 
categorised such as ‘objective and subjective’, ‘a priori an d a posteriori’ 
‘induction, deduction and abduction’ and ‘universality’? 2 In this context ‘spiritually’ has no relevance to religion. For an atheist country like China, 

‘spirituality’ relates to morality, ethics and virtues. 2  CULTURE THROUGH CHINESE THEORISING: HUMAN TRANSFORMING… 

