a photo of the object and a hint about the size of the object were located on each table in
the classroom. The tables in the classroom were arranged in a learning circle. During
task processing, students could fall back on three staged hints. The experimental
group could access them in the app, whereas in the classrooms, they were presented
on ﬂash cards on the different tables. After task processing, the experimental group
entered their result in the app and received direct feedback on its correctness. The
students in the classroom compared their results with the result on a ﬂash card. Both
groups could then read one solution to the problem—the experimental group in the
