conflicts, ruptures, breakdowns and tensions in  activity systems. As illustrated by the 
lightning-shaped arrows in Figure 4.6, in my study, contradictions emerged within 
and between (primary and secondary) the elem ents of the activity systems as well 
as between the main activity system and its neighbour activity system (quaternary). 65

