doctoral education process by supporting and sustaining student engagement. In our context, ‘culture’ refers to “the sum of activities – symbolic or instru-
mental – that exist in an organisation and create shared meaning” (Ti erney, 
1997:  3). The  same  author  describes  ‘socialisation’  as  the  “process  through 
which the individuals acquire and incorporate these activities” (1997: 3). For 
