improved access in the context of EFA, and the MDGs clearly had many dimen-
sions. CREATE aimed selectively to address six critical areas: (a) current patterns 
of access and exclusion in basic education, (b) strategies likely to be  most effective 
in meeting basic educational needs, (c) options available to improve student pro-
gression  in  and  completion  of  primary  educatio n,  (d)  addressing  dropout  and 
encouraging re-entry, (e) improving transition from primary to secondary level and 
(f)  political,  social  and  e conomic  conditions  under  which  the  EFA  goals  can  be 

