to wane. This is partly because the rules of the game may evolve during its
course. In the Cluedo game, the staff began swapping the cards they carried
among themselves so students could not tell which clues would be revealed. Some students formed their own teams and members targeted different staff
in the style of a megagame. The teams agreed to share the prize if they won. A similar school based a live event on Pelmanism. The staff donned badges
