professional, pre-calculus, culture-based pathway can be designed with a greater 
emphasis on need-to-know Platon ist content, compared to a full culture-based math-
ematics  curriculum  for  the  76%  majority  of  students. A  one-size-fits-all  conven-
tional curriculum does not represent twenty-first century realities (Russell 2016). Most students respond by “playing Fatima’s rules” (Aikenhead 2006, p. 28) to make 
