before  this  statement,  was  added  and  illustrated  some  less  serious  effects  of  the 
Pandemic. For  instance,  he  had  to  phone  the  doctor  instead  of  going  to  the  doctor’s 
ofﬁce  in  person. With  the  addition  of  an  emotionally  charged  comment,  we  can  see 
how  the  Pandemic  had  a  truly  profound  effect  on  Don—upsetting  his   regular  routine 
and  causing  discomfort  in  his  life. To  ﬁnd  via  narrative  inquiry,  a  story  of  an  elderly 
man’s  experience  of  engaging  in  an  art  practice,  and  how  he  was  able  to  ma intain 
his  resilience,  connectivity,  and  care  through  a  difﬁcult  and  the  most  “distressing” 
period  of  his  life,  is  a  valuable  insi ght. 6 Conclusion  

As  researchers,  our  aim  was  to  act  as  conduits  within  our  research  project,  connecting 
human  experience  during  the  P andemic  like  a  network  of  invisible  ﬁbers  running 
through  the  forest  ﬂoor—not  as  case  counts  on  a  graph—but  as  a  narrative  accoun t 
of  lived  experience. At  its  core,  “narrative  inquiry  is  people  in  relation  studying 
