products. Today, there is a growing body of research arguing the importance of more 
holistic learning across domains to support innovation. The Bauhaus approach is con-
sistent with Guile’s (2009) findings about the need to learn how the industry works as 
a  whole  in  the  contemporary   creative  arts  sector. The  Bauhaus  case  illustrates  an 
approach  that  empowers  learners  through  direct,  practical  experience  and  through 
exposure to different  ways of thinking and doing within the school and beyond it. Collaboration and Co-producing Innovation

