"How does the educator describe the differences between a creative classroom and a traditional one, particularly regarding the roles of discovery, questioning, and individual expression?","and  lead  me  to  a  future  creative  teaching  career. LASC  embraced  my  creativity, 
providing space that pushed discovery over standardized instruction. I discovered 
the art of teaching with passion, providing my students a chance to fall in love with 
several subjects. I developed my own teaching style. LASC encouraged me to create 
my own classes, providing opportunities for me to grow as a teacher and instructional 
designer. LASC noticed my purpose and nurtured it into existence. My work at LASC led to an early understanding of how to use creative instruction 
to  enhance  or  augment  learning  related  to  the  Common  Core   Standards. Classes 
I  developed  and  taught  included  Art-Science  Fusion,  a  course  series  for  middle 
