opportunities helped patients explain and work through pain, loss, sorrow, and grief. I was introduced to this research through work I was doing at the Markey Cancer 
Center while helping craft their proposal to become designated as a N ational Cancer 
Institute. At the time, the Markey Cancer Center had yet to implement creative arts 
and writing into its cancer therapy programs. Therefore, I explored the possibility of 
