•  Through  the  recruitment  process  of  faculty  and  students,  Ed.D. programs 
need to ensure that cultural responsiveness, social justice and equity are given 
considerations during the selection process. •  Cohort models lend themselves to the dynamic of the group. Ed.D. programs need 
to  provide  theory  supported  with  research  and  the  application  of  newly  learned 
competencies which doctoral students can use  in future educational leadership roles. •  Constructivist forums and collaborative opportunities focused on social justice 

and cultural responsiveness need to be woven throughout Ed.D. programs. •  Private universities have the sovereignty to commit to cultural responsiveness 
and social justice in their Ed.D. program curricula to empower future educational 
leaders with the competencies to engage the challenges of the ever-increasing 
diverse populations in  our school systems. •  Incorporating socially just and culturally responsive leadership is a continuous 

and on-going process requiring frequent checks and modifications . REFERENCES

