Culturally responsive and socially just leadership is based on educational equity for 
all students. Leaders who employ these leadership philosophies work to empower 
teachers, parents, and the community to meet the needs of the “cultural orientations  
of ethnically diverse students and their families” (Johnson, 2014, p. 149). The first guiding principle of the Carnegie Project on the Education Doctorate 
