The Challenges Confronting All People Living on the Planet Earth

This Epilogue is written to id entify the critical components and situations in the 
designs and purposes of education as the global force on the planet Earth in which 
human beings  live. It forms the concluding part of this book that provides not only 
a summary of the contents of the series of studies which precede it but also present s 
the  challenge  confronting  the  future  generations  of  people  living  in  the  World. Chapter  11  prepared  by  Esther  Ho  draws  attention  to  the  relationships  between 
education and human development and discusses the Capability  Approach to guide 
the analysis of the problems facing mankind. This is followed by a synthesis of the 
quality of basic education in the five Southeast Asian countries considered in this 
book in terms of Amartya  Sen’s work Development as Freedom (Sen, 1999). The  emphasis  on  education  is  potentially  the  driving  force  that  can  meet  the 
challenge and involve all people living in the World. The summary in the Preface of 
this current book states that “PISA assesses to what extent the 15-year-old students 
are  acquiring  key  knowledge  a nd  skills  that  are  essential  for  full  participation 
in modern societies”. PISA does not only test factual knowledge in the fields of 
Mathematics and Science. The PISA instruments assess the capabilities of Literacies 
in  Mathematics,  Science,  and  Reading. The  capabilities  involve  not  only  factual 
knowledge and problem solving that are aspects of the cognitive domain but also 
aspects of the affect ive domain that involves values, since education is no longer 
considered to be values-free or values-neutral. Carroll (1993) has investigated the 
