Australia. Nine ICS participants, selected by a snowball sampling method (Patton, 
2005) were interviewed about their adaptation to tertiary study in Australia i n order to 
identify any conflicts or tensions they had experienced. They were also interviewed 
about their family and schooling experiences in China. The theoretical perspective used was activity theory (Engeström, 1993, 2000a, 
2001),  particularly  an  adapted  Change  Laboratory  approach  (Enges tröm,  1991, 

