and vocational training must be broadened as a strategy integrating multiple 
educational activities in c ourses of different levels, from elementary school to 
graduate studies. PNPG must hence assume that vocational training, as a state 
policy, should articulate the skills required by the labor market and academia, 
as well  as open space for innovation, supporting the construction of hybrid 
teaching models which combine academic and professional spaces, different 
educat ional levels and institutions. From this perspective, professional courses, 
professional master’s programs and forthcoming professional doctorates will 
be reframed as components o f vocational education policies and strategies and 
articulated as an educational axis. (Brazil, 2010, p. 267)

