What type of future research is recommended to explore the long-term effects of working in an expert scientist identity on students' academic and career trajectories?,"They gained
a greater understanding of how science was connected to society, and science-based
careers. There were a few limitations in research design that may have impacted the ﬁnd-
ings. The research took place in one classroom over one term. This meant that the
data was often too small for substantive statistical analysis. In addition, the discon-
tinuous nature of this study may have impacted student engagement and scientist
identity formation, as the momentum was not a ble to be sustained. It would be useful
to undertake a longitudinal study to see if working in an expert scientist identity had
an impact over higher education in science  and career choices in the future. References

