tend to be missing from textbooks, because the body of knowledge 
described is unlinked from the tentative  stories of knowledge claims 
of  those who first generated it, and is now presented as factually cer-
tain. Therefore, no  arguments ( exposition) are needed and the  stories 
of how the knowledge was developed (a form of  narrative biography) 
