Accurately  assessing  the  peer  group  effect  is  a  difﬁcult  methodological  problem,  and 
the  biggest  cha llenge  is  the  bias  caused  by  the  self-selection  process  (Hoxby,  2002; 
Sacerdote,  2011). Families  will  have  their  children  “selectively”  enter  the  school

