they  prefer  for  many  reasons,  such  as  incom e,  place  of  residence,  choice  preference, 
and  so  on. It  means  that  students  can  choose  their  peers  subjectively  rather  than 
randomly  entering  into  peer  groups  of  schools  or  classes. The  self-selection  problem 
is  particularly  worthy  of  attention  in  this  paper. As  discussed  earlier,  compulsory 
education  in  China  is  not  selective  and  institutes  a  “nearby  enrollment  policy”  based 
