2016)  as  individual  ability  and  academic  performance  are  closely  related  to  family 
socioeconomic  status,  there  exists  a  common   phenomenon  that  the  more  excellent 
the  individual  is,  the  higher  performance  the  peers  have. Therefore,  if  we  ignored 
